{"name":"Baby’s Breath","hex":"#d8e4e8","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.","Any very young animal, especially a vertebrate; many species have specific names for their babies, such as kittens for the babies of cats, puppies for the babies of dogs, and chicks for the babies of birds. See Category:Baby animals for more."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"breath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or process of breathing.","A single act of breathing in or out; a breathing of air."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["voiceless, surd; contrasting with voice (breath sounds, voice sounds)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gypsophila","blocks":[{"text":"Gypsophila is a genus of flowering plants in the carnation family, Caryophyllaceae. They are native to Eurasia, Africa, Australia, and the Pacific Islands. Turkey has a particularly high diversity of Gypsophila taxa, with about 35 endemic species. Some Gypsophila are introduced species in other regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Gypsophila_repens_-_close-up_%28aka%29.jpg/330px-Gypsophila_repens_-_close-up_%28aka%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gypsophila","wikidata":"Q161948"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Gypsophila_repens_-_close-up_%28aka%29.jpg/500px-Gypsophila_repens_-_close-up_%28aka%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common